Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.

**Location: Bangalore**

***How you'll make an impact:***

Senior full-stack developers with knowledge of React and 5+ years of experience:

* Design and develop scalable front-end applications using React and JavaScript/TypeScript;
* Design and implement backend services, APIs, and integrations using Node.js;
* Develop and optimize database solutions using SQL, including complex queries and performance tuning;
* Diagnose complex application, integration, database, and production issues;
* Contribute to CI/CD, application security, performance, reliability, and production readiness;
* Provide technical guidance and mentoring to Junior and Middle developers.

**Middle full-stack Developers:**

* Develop and maintain front-end applications using React, JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, and CSS;
* Build and support backend services and REST APIs using Node.js;
* Design and develop database queries, stored procedures, and data integrations using SQL;
* Participate in application design, development, testing, deployment, and production support;
* Troubleshoot application defects and performance issues across the full technology stack;
* Participate in code reviews and collaborate with QA, Product, BA, and other engineering team members.

If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community — Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?

**Job ID:232836**

The Opportunity


Join our Acceleration Center India and help shape the future of business for our diverse client portfolio across geographies and jurisdictions. You’ll work at the heart of global teams across Advisory, Assurance, Tax and Business Services—solving real client challenges through connected collaboration. We’ll help you grow your skills so you can go further. With hands-on learning, cutting-edge tools and an inclusive culture, this is your opportunity to do inspiring work that makes a difference—every day.


As a Guidewire Policy Center Developer - Associate, you will develop and customize Guidewire PolicyCenter solutions within our Advisory practice, helping insurance clients improve policy administration and business application performance. At PwC Acceleration Center India, this role places you on a team that implements, enhances, and supports Guidewire systems through integrations, upgrades, and production improvements. You will contribute to designing, coding, and testing solutions shaped by client needs, using software development methods and digital tools while considering how PolicyCenter connects with ClaimCenter and BillingCenter. The team also applies automation and AI-supported approaches to improve operations and customer experiences.


As an Associate, you will build your technical and business understanding by contributing reliably to client projects and taking ownership of your work and development. As delivery needs change, you will use curiosity and analytical thinking to break down unfamiliar PolicyCenter challenges, ask questions, and adapt your approach. You will listen to different perspectives, communicate clearly with colleagues and clients, and use feedback to refine your work. By learning the firm’s technology resources and professional standards, you can develop your professional identity while helping the team deliver quality work.


**Responsibilities**

* Demonstrates advanced abilities providing solution strategy and Application Evolution Services (AES, formerly AMS) delivery as a Guidewire Lead Developer. Employees in the Lead Developer position should think of themselves and be regarded by the client as a trusted advisor and think strategically about how to create value using the Guidewire Suite of products;
* Demonstrates expert abilities delivering Guidewire application solutions as it will be critical that consultant in this position are capable of navigating both business processes as well as enterprise solution perspectives at high level and holistic view;
* Demonstrates expert abilities developing a scalable and robust Guidewire Solution Strategies in a hybrid IT landscape (on premises and Cloud);
* Demonstrates expert abilities and/or a proven record of success in developing independently new market-differentiated Guidewire solutions and leading proposal development efforts; Lead Developer in these positions should be capable of delivering Advisory-level work and be able to discuss future enhancements in Guidewire roadmap discussions with the client;
* Gathering client and team input to understand policy administration needs, clarify technical requirements, and connect assigned development tasks to broader insurance operations
* Developing and customizing Guidewire PolicyCenter features using established software development methods, with attention to maintainable code and the needs of deployed applications
* Configuring PolicyCenter workflows and assisting with Guidewire integrations involving BillingCenter and ClaimCenter, including BillingCenter configuration where policy and billing processes intersect
* Testing code and system changes, investigating defects, documenting findings, and revising solutions based on feedback from senior developers and client support teams
* Supporting deployed Guidewire applications by researching production issues, contributing to enhancements and upgrades, and using digital tools to track tasks and system performance
* Applying AI-enabled tools and automation with appropriate review to examine application behavior, organize technical findings, and identify opportunities for process improvements
* Collaborating with colleagues and client contacts through active listening, clear updates, and thoughtful responses to differing perspectives while seeking guidance on unfamiliar challenges
* Building technical knowledge through research and feedback, taking ownership of assigned deliverables, and adapting development approaches as client needs and project priorities change

What You Must Have



* Deep expertise in Guidewire PolicyCenter and good understanding of ClaimCenter, BillingCenter and ContactManager;
* GOSU, Guidewire Event and Rules Framework and Guidewire Web Services;
* Good Knowledge on XML & JSON formats and ANT, MAVEN, Gradle scripts;
* Experience using tools such as SOAP UI, Postman and working with code repositories such as SVN & GIT;
* At least a Bachelor's degree
* At least 2-4 years of experience
* Oral and written proficiency in English required

What Sets You Apart



* Demonstrates expert abilities leading global teams to generate a vision, establishing direction and motivating members, creating a community of high performing professional consultants, creating an atmosphere of trust, leveraging diverse views, coaching staff, and encouraging improvement and innovation;
* As a Lead Developer will be accountable for team of resources from both a utilization and learning perspective. Mentoring and helping to upskill junior resources will be critical in this role;
* Demonstrates intimate abilities and/or a proven record of success developing strategy as well as writing, communicating, facilitating, and presenting cogently; to and/or for all levels of industry audiences, clients and internal staff and management, such as presentation slides, practice marketing materials, change management plans and/or project plans, workshops and whitepapers, practice, methodologies and tools, policies and procedures, and/or other standard business communications;
* Be comfortable, thrive, and available during sustained period of time of instability with client's Guidewire solution and escalations; and,
* Key contributor and thought leader internally and externally with white papers, blogs, and training.
* Preference for at least one of the following fields of study: Actuarial Science, Business Administration/Management, Business Analytics, Commerce, Computer and Information Science, Computer Applications, Computer Engineering, Computer Engineering & Accounting, Data Processing/Analytics/Science, Economics, Electrical Engineering, Engineering, Engineering and Business, Finance, Information Technology, Management Information Systems, Mathematics, Mechanical Engineering, Operations Management/Research, Risk Management, Software App, Statistics
* At least one of the following: Guidewire and Scrum Master Certification
* Configuring Guidewire PolicyCenter to support insurance policy workflows
* Contributing to Guidewire integrations and software development tasks on client projects
* Applying feedback while troubleshooting deployed Guidewire solutions with team members

**Build better healthcare software for patients and professionals**

Script Assist is looking for a
**Product Designer**
to help shape the UX and UI of a growing suite of healthcare SaaS products.

We build technology used across the healthcare journey — from
**patient-facing digital experiences and mobile-responsive journeys to B2B SaaS platforms used by clinics, pharmacies and operational teams**
.

Our technology supports tens of thousands of prescriptions every month across multiple healthcare organisations and brands.

We’re looking for a Product Designer who combines
**strong UX thinking, excellent UI design, deep Figma capability and practical React/HTML/CSS experience**
.

This isn’t simply a role for making existing screens look better.

You’ll work on
**user journeys, interaction design, information architecture, complex workflows, design systems and production UI**
, helping us make sophisticated healthcare software clearer, simpler and more intuitive.

**What you’ll design**

You’ll work across both
**consumer-facing products and professional B2B SaaS applications**
.

That includes:

•       patient journeys;

•       responsive web and mobile experiences;

•       clinic software;

•       pharmacy software;

•       dashboards;

•       forms;

•       tables;

•       administrative workflows;

•       configuration interfaces;

•       information-dense applications;

•       customer-specific branded experiences.

You’ll need to think differently about a patient completing a simple journey on a phone and a professional user working inside complex software all day.

**What you’ll do**

As a Product Designer, you’ll:

•       design end-to-end user journeys and user flows;

•       improve UX across existing software products;

•       simplify complex workflows;

•       create wireframes, prototypes and high-fidelity UI in Figma;

•       design intuitive web application and mobile-responsive experiences;

•       work on information architecture and interaction design;

•       build and evolve reusable Figma components and design systems;

•       create scalable UI patterns, components, variants and design tokens;

•       design dashboards, forms, tables and information-dense SaaS interfaces;

•       collaborate directly with Product and Engineering;

•       work within existing React applications;

•       use HTML/CSS and React knowledge to support or implement front-end design changes;

•       review implemented features and maintain a high standard of UI quality;

•       help create and maintain customer-specific themes and white-labelled experiences.

**International product experience**

Our software is designed primarily for UK and international users.

We’re therefore specifically looking for Product Designers whose professional experience has
**predominantly involved designing software for international customers or end users outside India**
.

That could mean working:

•       for an international software company;

•       for an Indian SaaS company serving international markets;

•       on international B2B SaaS products;

•       in product teams serving UK, European, US or other international customers.

**What we’re looking for**

You should have:

•       at least
**2 years of professional Product Design / UX/UI experience**
;

•       at least
**2 years of professional Figma experience**
;

•       at least
**2 years of practical React experience**
;

•       practical HTML/CSS experience;

•       experience designing real software products;

•       strong UX fundamentals;

•       experience with user journeys, user flows and interaction design;

•       experience with responsive web application design;

•       experience with Figma components and design systems;

•       experience working closely with software engineers;

•       a Bachelor’s degree or higher in Engineering, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology or another relevant technical discipline;

•       a strong Product Design portfolio.

**Particularly interesting backgrounds**

We’d especially like to hear from Product Designers with experience in:

•       SaaS;

•       B2B SaaS;

•       B2B2C products;

•       enterprise software;

•       healthcare technology;

•       fintech;

•       complex workflows;

•       information-dense applications;

•       configurable software;

•       multi-tenant SaaS;

•       white-label products;

•       consumer and professional software;

•       design systems.

You do not need experience in all of these areas.

**What matters to us**

We’re looking for somebody who thinks beyond individual screens. You should be interested in:

•       why users behave the way they do;

•       why a journey feels difficult;

•       how information should be structured;

•       how a complex workflow can feel simple;

•       how components behave across an entire product;

•       how a design will actually be implemented in software.

You should care about visual quality, but understand that great Product Design is fundamentally about creating software that
**works brilliantly for the people using it**
.

**Working with Script Assist**

This is a full-time India role.

You’ll initially work remotely, with the role expected to move towards hybrid working from our Ahmedabad team hub in future.

You’ll work closely with Product and Engineering on software used by real healthcare organisations, operational teams and patients.

If you’re a Product Designer who combines
**UX/UI, Figma, design systems and React/front-end understanding**
, we’d love to see what you’ve built.

**About AppDirect**

Become a digital, global citizen and enable the new generation of digital entrepreneurs around the world. AppDirect offers a subscription commerce platform to sell any product, through any channel, on any device - as a service. We power millions of subscriptions worldwide for organizations. We do this by our values-driven culture—one that enables you to Be Seen, Be Yourself, and Do Your Best Work.  

**About You**

AppDirect is looking for a Senior Manager, Software Development to lead our Core Billing Team in Pune. You will play a critical role in guiding a team of talented engineers, driving technical excellence, and shaping Billing's product direction. You'll help your team of Senior career engineers navigate shifting priorities with clarity and confidence, ensuring high-quality delivery and strong alignment with business goals.

You are equally excited about software development and people development. As a hands-on leader, you provide clear, actionable feedback on technical designs, and can contribute directly to development when needed.

You bring that same hands-on approach to AI: you have worked with AI coding assistants or agentic development tools yourself, see them as a lever for both how your team builds and what we deliver to customers, and know how to help experienced engineers adopt them in a way that raises quality, not just speed. You evolve your team's practices across requirements, design, review and testing as coding gets faster. In a billing system, accuracy is non-negotiable, so you keep human judgment and accountability at the center, hold AI-generated code to the same bar as any other, and use only approved tools to protect company code and customer data.

If you're a collaborative, product-minded leader who thrives in dynamic environments, brings out the best in others, and believes that great teams build great products—your next challenge starts here.

**What you'll do and how you'll have an impact**

* Lead, support and mentor a team made up of experienced Full Stack Developers. You will own performance management for your team (i.e. objectives setting, performance reviews and career development) as well as recruitment and overall team management;
* Coach engineers by reviewing technical designs and code, conducting technical talks, and advocating for best practices;
* Guide the team in the design, implementation, observability and support of an ecosystem of fault-tolerant services to minimize customer impact in case of failures;
* Be a quality, performance and security evangelist to your team;
* Understand the system from end to end to help the team make tradeoff decisions;
* Partner with the Product Manager, Designer, and other Engineering Managers and Tech Leads to collaborate and build the best billing experience anywhere;
* Communicate clearly any risks and provide resolution or mitigation plans;
* Act as a sounding board and motivator for individual creativity on technical challenges, process efficiencies and everything in between;
* Stay hands-on with the team by contributing to non-critical path code improvements and maintaining a deep understanding of the platform's technical landscape.
* Lead your team's adoption of AI-assisted and agentic development using approved tools, and evolve team processes (requirements, design, review, testing) as coding gets faster;
* Set review standards for AI-generated code: every change gets human review for correctness, security and performance, which matters most in billing, where accuracy is non-negotiable;
* Enforce security and IP guardrails: approved tools only, and no company code or customer and billing data sent to unvetted AI services;
* Measure the impact of AI on delivery, focusing on cycle time, quality and incidents (with AI-assisted pull requests as a supporting adoption signal), and use the data to coach the team and report to leadership.

**What we're looking for**

* 12+ years in Software Development and minimum 5 years in people management;
* Proven experience managing teams of 10+ developers and delivering highly reliable customer-focused products;
* Strong technical expertise in back-end and front-end development technologies, including Java, Node.js, SQL, and API frameworks like GraphQL;
* Solid understanding of scalable system architecture and best practices, including API design, event-based communications, asynchronous flows, eventual consistency, observability, and tooling;
* Experience in leading investigation of complex production issues;
* Excellent communication skills in English, both oral and written, with the ability to engage both technical and non-technical audiences;
* Experience with Agile development processes and cross-functional collaboration;
* Hands-on experience with AI coding assistants or agentic development tools, and experience leading a team to adopt them;
* Familiarity with how LLM-based features are built (e.g. RAG, tool calling, evaluation) and with AI security, privacy and IP risks; experience shipping AI-powered features is a plus.

*At AppDirect, we believe that innovation thrives in an environment that houses diversity of excellence, experience and thought. We respect each AppDirector as their own fingerprint; unique with no one alike. We foster an environment of inclusion without regard to race, religion, age, sexual orientation, or gender identity enabling AppDirectors to embrace their uniqueness to do their best work. As such, we strongly encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized people, people with disabilities, people from gender and sexually diverse communities, and/or people with intersectional identities.*

*At AppDirect we take privacy very seriously. For more information about our use and handling of personal data from job applicants, please read our Candidate Privacy Policy. For more information of our general privacy practices, please see AppDirect Privacy Notice: https://www.appdirect.com/about/privacy-notice*

*At AppDirect, AI tools may assist our recruitment team with administrative automations — always under human oversight. AI tools do not make hiring decisions or solely automated decisions about your candidacy – all decisions are made by our people. By submitting your application, you acknowledge that your information may be processed in this way. You may request access or deletion at any time by contacting* *privacy@appdirect.com**.*

In 2026, Averna and Spherea joined forces to form the Spherea Group.  A global Test & Quality Solution leader, Averna Powered by Spherea partners with product designers, developers and manufacturers to help them achieve higher product quality, accelerate time to market and protect their brands by covering and offering solutions and expertise for the entire product lifecycle.


Averna Powered by Spherea offers specialized expertise and innovative test, vision inspection, precision assembly and automated solutions that deliver substantial technical, financial and market benefits for clients in the aerospace, automotive, consumer electronics, defense, energy, industrials, medical devices & life sciences, semiconductor, telecom and transportation industries.


Their solutions include prototyping & consulting, precision assembly & production, automated test solutions, in-line test systems, test system replication, and test platforms & products. Averna Powered by Spherea’s expertise ranges from vision systems, specialized battery test, RF & microwave and fiber optics to robotics & motion, instrumentation, control systems, and data management.


**Job Description**
**Position Overview**
The Account Manager role is responsible for developing top-tier accounts in India.This role blends complex technical problems, a consultative solution-based selling culture and exposure to world-renowned technology organizations we proudly call our customers. The ideal candidate will have a solid technical background in engineering fields such as mechanical, automation, electrical, or electronics, and a proven ability to develop and implement sales strategies for complex technical solutions. This highly visible, cross-functional role is a great opportunity to showcase your skills within all departments of Averna and across the globe.


**The successful candidate will:**

* Identify/ Develop New Business focusing on Test System Integration (design, replication, support) in Averna’s target industries;
* Maintain/grow existing accounts;
* Build/execute/report on account plans through collaboration with internal teams (Marketing, Operations, etc.);
* Present Solution concepts and Business proposals to our customers;
* Manage opportunities by leveraging strong relationships you build with Averna’s world-class pre-sales teams.
* Define account strategies and execute sales plan
* Manage Salesforce CRM to maintain the sales funnel, forecast sales, and generate accurate sales reports.

**Qualifications**
**The ideal candidate in a few words:**
**Education & Technical Expertise**

* Bachelor’s degree in engineering (Mechanical, Optical, Electrical preferred);
* Solid understanding of engineering design and manufacturing processes;
* Technical understanding of automation, test, and measurement equipment concepts;
* Experience with automation applications, including precision mechanics and optical systems;

**Sales & Account Management Experience**

* 5+ years of experience in custom automation solution selling, including Test & Measurement solutions for Manufacturing Industry;
* Demonstrated experience in consultative technology solution selling of capital equipment to OEMs/CMs;
* Business development of key accounts, including qualifying customers for Averna’s capabilities and driving internal teams to meet customer requirements;
* Account planning and management;
* Track record of annual sales in the millions/ year range
* Excellent communication, negotiation, and relationship-building skills.
* Familiarity with the National Instruments toolset a plus
* PLC Beckhoff based automation selling a plus

**Work Style & Logistics**

* Onsite/Hybrid work style;
* Ability to travel up to 70% of the time (travel domestically and internationally as needed).

**Additional Information**
**What's in it for YOU:**

* A dynamic sales role with direct exposure to world-class technology organizations;
* Be part of a global team with a strong and collaborative work culture;
* A highly visible, cross-functional position that highlights your expertise across all Averna departments and global markets;
* Competitive benefits package;
* Opportunities to travel ;
* Be part of a company that puts ESG at the heart of its mission, for people, planet, and performance.

Averna is committed to employment equity and to encouraging diversity and inclusion. We are pleased to consider all qualified applicants for employment, regardless of race, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.

